1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,880
America's air traffic control
美国的空中交通管制，

2
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:03,860
still runs partly on floppy disks.
有一部分还在用软盘。

3
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:07,100
The FAA says floppies carry weather and other key information
美国联邦航空局说，四百多个空管设施

4
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:09,190
at more than four hundred facilities.
靠软盘传天气等关键信息。

5
00:00:09,190 --> 00:00:10,150
This week it promised
这周它承诺：

6
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:12,650
to phase them out by the end of twenty twenty eight.
2028 年底前全部淘汰。

7
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:15,370
Floppies mostly vanished more than twenty five years ago,
软盘早在二十五年前就基本没人用了，

8
00:00:15,370 --> 00:00:17,980
and have not been mass produced since twenty eleven.
2011 年后也不再大量生产。

9
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:20,280
Reuters reports that some replacement parts
路透社报道，有些替换零件，

10
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:21,470
were bought on eBay.
是从 eBay 上买的。

11
00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:24,160
Today's brain teaser: how does a thin piece of plastic
今天的烧脑问题：一片薄薄的塑料，

12
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:25,520
remember anything at all?
凭什么能记住东西？

13
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:26,670
Meet our hero, Floppy:
认识主角：小软，

14
00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:29,250
one point four four megabytes of pure attitude.
一点四四兆字节的倔脾气。

15
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:30,910
One point four four megabytes
一点四四兆字节，

16
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:32,580
is roughly one phone photo.
大约就是一张手机照片。

17
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:35,340
Your phone might hold two hundred fifty six gigabytes.
你的手机也许有二百五十六 G，

18
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:38,790
By our math, that is about one hundred seventy thousand Floppies.
我们算了下，相当于十七万张软盘。

19
00:00:38,790 --> 00:00:41,380
Twist one: inside, there is no paper and no ink.
反转一：里面没有纸，也没有墨，

20
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:43,880
Just a thin disk coated with a kind of rust.
只有一张涂着“铁锈”的薄圆片。

21
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:45,970
That rust is packed with tiny magnets,
这层铁锈里全是小磁铁，

22
00:00:45,970 --> 00:00:47,240
far too small to see.
小到看不见。

23
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:49,530
Each tiny patch points one way or the other.
每一小块，磁铁要么朝这边，要么朝那边：

24
00:00:49,530 --> 00:00:51,950
One way means one, the other way means zero.
一边是一，一边是零。

25
00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:53,030
Like a stadium crowd
就像体育场里的观众，

26
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:55,540
flipping cards up or down to make a picture.
举牌子朝上或朝下，拼出一幅画。

27
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:57,220
Spin the disk, and a little head
圆片一转，一个小磁头

28
00:00:57,220 --> 00:00:59,870
flips the magnets as they pass. That is writing.
就把经过的小磁铁一块块翻过来，这就是写。

29
00:00:59,870 --> 00:01:00,990
Reading is the reverse:
读正好反过来：小磁铁经过线圈，

30
00:01:00,990 --> 00:01:03,630
passing magnets nudge a tiny current through a coil.
推出一点点电流。

31
00:01:03,630 --> 00:01:05,310
Twist two: magnets are stubborn.
反转二：磁铁很倔，

32
00:01:05,310 --> 00:01:07,310
Leave them alone, and they stay put.
你不碰它，它就一直这么指着。

33
00:01:07,310 --> 00:01:09,200
Some rocks have kept their magnetism
有些岩石里的磁性，

34
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:10,480
for millions of years.
保存了几百万年。

35
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,810
So why replace floppies?
那为啥要换掉软盘？

36
00:01:11,810 --> 00:01:15,160
Twist three: the disk is fine; the world around it is not.
反转三：盘没坏，是它周围的世界变了。

37
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:17,020
Drives wear out. Heads get dirty.
驱动器会磨损，磁头会脏，

38
00:01:17,020 --> 00:01:18,610
And nobody makes new ones.
而且没人再造新的了。

39
00:01:18,610 --> 00:01:20,040
Bring a strong magnet close,
一块强磁铁靠近，

40
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:22,140
and the weather data can get scrambled.
天气数据就可能乱掉。

41
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:22,840
Plastic ages,
放久了，塑料会老，

42
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:24,950
and that rusty coating can flake off.
那层“铁锈”也可能脱落。

43
00:01:24,950 --> 00:01:26,220
And speed: by our estimate,
还有速度：我们估算，

44
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:28,310
reading a whole disk takes about a minute.
读完一整张大约要一分钟。

45
00:01:28,310 --> 00:01:30,230
The FAA's chief put it this way:
航空局局长说：

46
00:01:30,230 --> 00:01:31,860
every facility is a silo.
“每个设施都是一座孤岛。”

47
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:33,900
When data cannot flow over a network,
数据没法在网上流动，

48
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:35,350
someone has to carry it.
就得有人拿着它走。

49
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:37,060
The plan: one new display system
新计划：一套新的显示系统，

50
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:39,790
replaces four systems from the nineteen eighties.
一口气替换四套八十年代的老系统。

51
00:01:39,790 --> 00:01:42,990
Congress approved twelve and a half billion dollars last year,
国会去年批了一百二十五亿美元，

52
00:01:42,990 --> 00:01:46,160
and the transportation secretary wants thirty billion more.
交通部长还想再要三百亿。

53
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:48,060
Paper flight strips are retiring too:
纸质的飞行进程单也要退休：

54
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:50,860
twenty seven big airports have already dropped them.
二十七个大机场已经不用了。

55
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:51,490
Why so slow?
为啥这么慢？

56
00:01:51,490 --> 00:01:53,920
You cannot switch off the sky to upgrade it.
天空没法关机升级。

57
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:55,590
It is like swapping a plane's engine
就像飞机还在天上飞，

58
00:01:55,590 --> 00:01:56,870
while it is still flying.
你得给它换发动机。

59
00:01:56,870 --> 00:01:58,880
Fine print: old does not mean unsafe.
友情提示：老，不等于不安全。

60
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,950
These machines have run for decades.
这些机器跑了几十年。

61
00:02:00,950 --> 00:02:02,940
But hunting for spare parts on eBay
但从 eBay 上淘零件，

62
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:04,430
is not a long term plan.
可不是长久之计。

63
00:02:04,430 --> 00:02:05,710
And here is the irony:
还有个讽刺的事：

64
00:02:05,710 --> 00:02:08,610
big data centers still archive on magnetic tape.
大型数据中心今天还在用磁带存档。

65
00:02:08,610 --> 00:02:09,780
Same trick as Floppy:
跟小软一个道理：

66
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:12,350
tiny magnets, pointing one way or the other.
小磁铁，朝上或朝下。

67
00:02:12,350 --> 00:02:14,030
So how does plastic remember?
所以塑料凭什么能记住东西？

68
00:02:14,030 --> 00:02:16,530
It does not. Millions of tiny magnets do.
它记不住，是上千万个小磁铁在记。

69
00:02:16,530 --> 00:02:18,570
Floppy is not retiring because it forgot.
小软退休，不是因为它忘了。

70
00:02:18,570 --> 00:02:21,750
It is retiring because everyone forgot how to talk to it.
是因为大家都忘了怎么跟它说话。

